# s2b-remote-file-reader core wiring

## 1. Modules
mixdog-connections/src/lib.rs, after `pub mod link;`, add:
    pub mod remote_file_reader;
The test module is declared inside remote_file_reader.rs (`remote_file_reader_tests.rs`).

## 2. Cargo
mixdog-connections/Cargo.toml [dependencies], add (the workspace member exists in native/core/Cargo.toml as `mixdog-workspace = { path = "crates/mixdog-workspace" }`):
    mixdog-workspace = { workspace = true }
No reverse edge: no manifest under crates/ except mixdog-connections' own names mixdog-connections, so mixdog-workspace cannot reach it (no cycle).
No new external crate. Cargo.lock: the `mixdog-connections` package gains `"mixdog-workspace"` in its dependency list.

## 3. SERVICE_PENDING
Serves no protocol method; nothing to remove.

## 4. Compose
Where the daemon builds `ServerDownloads::begin(reader, ...)` for a server window: `link_pool.reader(&connection_id)`
(`LinkPool::reader(&self, server_id: &str) -> Option<Arc<dyn mixdog_workspace::RemoteFileReader>>`, `None` when no link is held: the caller answers
the not-connected refusal it already uses for any server call).
